# 1. DC01 Network Configuration

DC01 was deployed into the dedicated server subnet:

```text
snet-servers
10.10.10.0/24
```

The virtual machine was intentionally deployed **without a public IP address**.

This prevents direct Internet-based administrative access to the domain controller.

Administrative access is performed through the management server:

```text
Administrator Workstation
        |
        | RDP
        v
     MGMT01
  10.10.1.x
        |
        | RDP / Management
        v
     DC01
  10.10.10.4
```

This design separates the management plane from the server infrastructure.

---

# 2. Network Security Group

DC01 is protected by the server subnet Network Security Group:

```text
nsg-servers
```

Management traffic was restricted to the management subnet.

### Configured Rules

| Priority | Rule                   | Source         | Destination Port | Protocol | Action |
| -------: | ---------------------- | -------------- | ---------------: | -------- | ------ |
|      100 | Allow-RDP-Management   | `10.10.1.0/24` |             3389 | TCP      | Allow  |
|      110 | Allow-WinRM-Management | `10.10.1.0/24` |             5985 | TCP      | Allow  |

No Internet-to-DC01 RDP rule was created.

This follows the principle of restricting administrative access to a controlled management network.

