# 7. DNS Configuration and Verification

Active Directory Domain Services was installed with integrated DNS.

DC01's IPv4 address:

```text
10.10.10.4
```

The DNS client configuration showed the local loopback address:

```text
127.0.0.1
```

The IPv6 loopback address was also observed:

```text
::1
```

These addresses indicate that DC01 is resolving DNS queries through its own DNS service.

The local DNS configuration was not unnecessarily modified after successful domain resolution was confirmed.

---

# 8. DNS Troubleshooting

### Test 1 — Domain Resolution

```powershell
nslookup corp.securecloud.local
```

Result:

```text
Name:    corp.securecloud.local
Address: 10.10.10.4
```

This confirmed that the Active Directory domain could be resolved through DNS.

### Test 2 — Domain Controller Resolution

```powershell
nslookup dc01.corp.securecloud.local
```

Result:

```text
Name:    dc01.corp.securecloud.local
Address: 10.10.10.4
```

This confirmed that the domain controller's fully qualified domain name resolved correctly.

### `Unknown / ::1` Observation

`nslookup` reported:

```text
Server:  Unknown
Address: ::1
```

Although this initially appeared concerning, the actual DNS lookup successfully returned:

```text
corp.securecloud.local
10.10.10.4
```

Therefore, the `Unknown / ::1` output was not treated as a DNS failure.

